---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import MotionStage from '@/components/motion/MotionStage.astro';
import MotionUsage from '@/components/motion/MotionUsage.astro';
import MotionOptions from '@/components/motion/MotionOptions.astro';
import MotionTokens from '@/components/motion/MotionTokens.astro';
import Inbox from '@/components/motion/scenes/Inbox.astro';
import InboxControls from '@/components/motion/scenes/InboxControls.astro';
import { MotionListReact } from '@/examples/react/motion-list.tsx';
import { MotionListAngular } from '@/examples/angular/motion-list.ts';
import MotionListSvelte from '@/examples/svelte/motion-list.svelte';
import { chipClass } from '@/components/motionDemo';
---
<MotionPage
  slug="lists"
  title="Motion: make a list appear"
  description="Items added together cascade in visual order; a leaving item lets its neighbours close the gap. In HTML, React, Angular and Svelte."
>
  <MotionStage scene="inbox" label="Live example: Make a list appear" height="md">
    <Fragment slot="controls"><InboxControls size="page" /></Fragment>
    <Inbox />
    <Fragment slot="readout"><span class={`${chipClass} tracking-normal`} data-inbox-readout>origin: 'first' · stagger: 'normal' · exit: 'out-of-flow'</span></Fragment>
  </MotionStage>

  <h2>How to use it</h2>
  <p>
    A list item names two motions: a presence, which makes it enter and leave, and <code>reflow</code>, which makes it
    follow its neighbours. The preset <code>cascade</code> is a presence with <code>stagger: 'normal'</code>.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`<ul>
  <li data-motion="cascade reflow"><span>One</span></li>
  <li data-motion="cascade reflow"><span>Two</span></li>
</ul>`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Items that enter in the same task start one step after the previous one, in visual order. Each framework renders
    the list as it renders any list: a keyed loop, with the presence on each item. In React, a <code>&lt;Presence&gt;</code>
    around the loop keeps a removed item rendered until its exit has played.
  </p>

  <h2>Use it in the frameworks</h2>
  <p>The live examples add a message at the top, and dismiss a message with its button. A message that leaves plays its exit before the list lets it go.</p>
  <MotionUsage name="motion-list">
    <MotionListReact slot="react" client:visible />
    <MotionListAngular slot="angular" client:visible />
    <MotionListSvelte slot="svelte" client:visible />
  </MotionUsage>

  <h2>Stagger and exit</h2>
  <p>
    <code>stagger</code> sets the step between the elements that enter together: <code>tight</code> (20 ms),
    <code>normal</code> (50 ms) or <code>loose</code> (100 ms), capped at 400 ms in all. Entries and exits cascade apart.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>origin</code> sets where the cascade starts: <code>first</code>, <code>last</code>, or <code>center</code>,
    which spreads both ways from the middle.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>exit</code> sets how a leaving element moves its neighbours. <code>in-place</code> keeps it where it is until its
    exit has played. <code>out-of-flow</code> takes it out of the flow when the exit starts, so the messages below close
    the gap while it fades.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`import { defineMotion } from '@udixio/motion';

defineMotion('list-item', {
  verb: 'appear',
  keyframes: [{ opacity: 0, y: 16 }, { opacity: 1, y: 0 }],
  stagger: 'normal',
  origin: 'first',
  exit: 'out-of-flow',
});`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Options</h2>
  <MotionOptions verb="appear" />

  <h2>Timing and tokens</h2>
  <p>The messages use the default spring, and the steps of the cascade come from the stagger tokens.</p>
  <MotionTokens tokens={['spring.default.spatial', 'stagger.normal']} />

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The entry is a short fade, and the cascade has no delays: the messages appear together.</li>
    <li>The exit is <code>in-place</code>, whatever the option says.</li>
    <li>Set <code>--udx-motion: none</code> on the list to show the end state at once.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>out-of-flow</code> needs a positioned parent: the list is <code>relative</code>.</li>
    <li>The cascade is capped at 400 ms, however many items enter together.</li>
  </ul>
</MotionPage>
